1
00:00:01,929 --> 00:00:07,246
(Q31) Producing enough energy to meet our needs has become a serious problem.

2
00:00:07,246 --> 00:00:15,314
[Q31答案句] Demand is rising rapidly, because of the world's increasing population and expanding industry.

3
00:00:15,314 --> 00:00:24,597
(Q32) Burning fossil fuels, like gas, coal and oil, seriously damages the environment and they'll eventually run out.

4
00:00:24,597 --> 00:00:36,853
For a number of years now, scientists have been working out how we can derive energy from renewable sources, such as the sun and wind, without causing pollution.

5
00:00:36,853 --> 00:00:47,951
Today I'll outline marine renewable energy - also called ocean energy - which harnesses the movement of the oceans.

6
00:00:47,951 --> 00:01:04,593
Marine renewable energy can be divided into three main categories: wave energy, tidal energy and ocean thermal energy conversion, and I'll say a few words about each one.

7
00:01:04,593 --> 00:01:07,688
First, wave energy.

8
00:01:07,688 --> 00:01:23,692
Numerous devices have been invented to harvest wave energy, with names such as Wave Dragon, the Penguin and Mighty Whale, and research is going on to try and come up with a really efficient method.

9
00:01:23,692 --> 00:01:33,774
[Q32答案句，答案前置， adj+n. = n. +be + adj] This form of energy has plenty of potential, as the source is constant, and there's no danger of waves coming to a standstill.

10
00:01:33,774 --> 00:01:43,025
(Q33) Electricity can be generated using onshore systems, using a reservoir, or offshore systems.

11
00:01:43,025 --> 00:01:52,480
[Q33答案句] But the problem with ocean waves is that they're erratic, with the wind making them travel in every direction.

12
00:01:52,480 --> 00:02:05,046
(Q34) This adds to the difficulty of creating efficient technology: ideally all the waves would travel smoothly and regularly along the same straight line.

13
00:02:05,046 --> 00:02:17,305
[Q34答案句] Another drawback is that sand and other sediment on the ocean floor might be stopped from flowing normally, which can lead to environmental problems.

14
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:24,056
(Q35) The second category of marine energy that I'll mention is tidal energy.

15
00:02:24,056 --> 00:02:39,177
[Q35答案句] One major advantage of using the tide, rather than waves, as a source of energy is that it's predictable: we know the exact times of high and low tides for years to come.

16
00:02:39,177 --> 00:02:55,292
(Q36) For tidal energy to be effective, the difference between high and low tides needs to be at least five metres, and this occurs naturally in only about forty places on Earth.

17
00:02:55,292 --> 00:03:06,250
But the right conditions can be created by constructing a tidal lagoon, an area of sea water separated from the sea.

18
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:12,948
One current plan is to create a tidal lagoon on the coast of Wales.

19
00:03:12,948 --> 00:03:24,320
[Q36答案句] This will be an area of water within a bay at Swansea, sheltered by a U-shaped breakwater, or dam, built out from the coast.

20
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:40,873
(Q37) The breakwater will contain sixteen hydro turbines, and as the tide rises, water rushes through the breakwater, activating the turbines, which turn a generator to produce electricity.

21
00:03:40,873 --> 00:03:56,481
Then, for three hours as the tide goes out, the water is held back within the break water, increasing the difference in water level, until it's several metres higher within the lagoon than in the open sea.

22
00:03:56,481 --> 00:04:04,770
[Q37答案句] Then, in order to release the stored water, gates in the breakwater are opened.

23
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:17,846
It pours powerfully out of the lagoon, driving the turbines in the breakwater in the opposite direction and again generating thousands of megawatts of electricity.

24
00:04:17,846 --> 00:04:37,970
(Q38) As there are two high tides a day, this lagoon scheme would generate electricity four times a day, every day, for a total of around 14 hours in every 24 - and enough electricity for over 150,000 homes.

25
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:55,807
[Q38答案句] This system has quite a lot in its favour: unlike solar and wind energy it doesn't depend on the weather; the turbines are operated without the need for fuel, so it doesn't create any greenhouse gas emissions; and very little maintenance is needed.

26
00:04:55,807 --> 00:05:10,761
(Q39) [Q39答案句] It's estimated that electricity generated in this way will be relatively cheap, and that manufacturing the components would create more than 2,000 jobs, a big boost to the local economy.

27
00:05:10,761 --> 00:05:26,870
(Q40) [Q40答案句] On the other hand, there are fears that lagoons might harm both fish and birds, for example by disturbing migration patterns, and causing a build-up of silt, affecting local ecosystems.

28
00:05:26,870 --> 00:05:37,591
There are other forms of tidal energy, but I'll go on to the third category of marine energy: ocean thermal energy conversion.

29
00:05:37,591 --> 00:05:52,733
This depends on there being a big difference in temperature between surface water and the water a couple of kilometres below the surface, and this occurs in tropical coastal areas.

30
00:05:52,733 --> 00:06:00,076
The idea is to bring cold water up to the surface using a submerged pipe.

31
00:06:00,076 --> 00:06:02,576
The concept dates back to 1881, when ...

